---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/content';
import { site } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="About & contact"
  ><section class="container page-intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">About & contact</span><h1>
      Michael Simkin.<br /><em>Independent AI researcher.</em>
    </h1><p>{site.introduction}</p>
  </section><section class="container about-layout">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>From computer vision to broader AI research</h2><p>
        Computer vision was my main research interest for many years. As the field of AI has
        evolved, my interests have broadened beyond vision. Recently I have been exploring
        AI-assisted mathematical proofs.
      </p><h2>Building the tools to ask a question</h2><p>
        My work ranges from Conway’s Game of Life constructions to mathematical research and
        software experiments. This site collects those interests through articles about specific
        results and projects.
      </p><p>
        For the glider-gun search, I wanted a simple approach: place a few potential catalysts and
        search the combinations. Making that practical meant first building the infrastructure,
        LifeAPI and CatForce.
      </p><p>
        Some work here is demonstrated, some is experimental, and some remains a candidate claim.
        Each article makes that distinction explicit and links to the public material behind it.
      </p><h2>Explore the work</h2><p>
        Start with an <a href={href('interests/')}>interest</a>, or browse the <a
          href={href('#articles')}>recent articles</a
        >. The categories are different ways into the same collection.
      </p><h2>Contact</h2><p>My public code and project documentation are on GitHub.</p><div
        class="about-links"
      >
        <a href={site.github}>simsim314 on GitHub ↗</a>{
          site.email && <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
        }{site.arxiv && <a href={site.arxiv}>arXiv profile ↗</a>}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section></Base
>
